# Clean Code

Working code is not automatically clean code. Preserve behavior; leave touched code cleaner within scope.

## Decision rules
- One responsibility per function; keep methods small and at one abstraction level
- Precise names; one term per concept; no abbreviations like `tmp`, `data2`
- Few meaningful parameters; avoid boolean flags and grab-bag args
- Commands vs queries; no hidden side effects
- Happy path first; isolate validation/errors; don't swallow exceptions
- Keep JavaFX, JPA/DB, and PDF details out of domain calculation (`PayrollCalculator` / services)
- Comments for why/constraints only; delete commented-out code
- Tests are production code; protect changed behavior

## When editing
- Split mixed setup/validation/compute/side-effect methods
- If cleanup spreads, stop at the smallest safe refactor for the request
- Prefer existing `controller` → `service` → `repository` layers; ask before adding new layers
- When changing behavior, update or add a test; run tests when the user asks or when shipping a fix
